## Summary

`normalize_codex_jsonl()` in `src/backend/output_normalizer.rs` parses the wrong JSON shape, causing every Codex backend call to fail and fall back to the Claude Sonnet reformatter. Fix it to correctly parse the agentic event format that `codex exec --json` actually emits.

## Context

The normalizer currently looks for `{"role": "assistant", "content": "..."}` but real Codex output is a JSONL stream of typed events. The assistant response is at `item.type == "agent_message"` → `item.text`.

## Requirements

**File to modify:** `src/backend/output_normalizer.rs`, function `normalize_codex_jsonl()` (lines 113–201)

### Parsing changes

1. Extract `thread_id` from `{"type":"thread.started","thread_id":"..."}` events → map to `session_id`
2. Extract assistant text from `{"type":"item.completed","item":{"type":"agent_message","text":"..."}}` — use the **last** such event if multiple exist
3. Extract usage from `{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{...}}`:
   - `input_tokens` → `tokens_in`
   - `output_tokens` → `tokens_out`
   - `cached_input_tokens` → `cached_in` (field name differs from other backends)
4. Retain the existing `{"role":"assistant","content":"..."}` path as a secondary fallback (do not remove it)

### Unit test to add

Add the following test to the existing test module in `output_normalizer.rs`:

```rust
#[test]
fn codex_real_jsonl_extracts_text_and_session() {
    let jsonl = r#"{"type":"thread.started","thread_id":"019c6e78-abc"}
{"type":"turn.started"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"reasoning","text":"thinking..."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"# Implementation Notes\n\nDone."}}
{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":8790,"cached_input_tokens":6784,"output_tokens":24}}"#;
    let result = normalize_output("codex", jsonl).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(result.text, "# Implementation Notes\n\nDone.");
    assert_eq!(result.session_id.as_deref(), Some("019c6e78-abc"));
    assert_eq!(result.tokens_in, Some(8790));
    assert_eq!(result.tokens_out, Some(24));
    assert_eq!(result.cached_in, Some(6784));
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `normalize_codex_jsonl` extracts `thread_id` from `type:thread.started` events into `session_id`
- [ ] `normalize_codex_jsonl` extracts text from `type:item.completed` + `item.type:agent_message`, using the last occurrence
- [ ] `normalize_codex_jsonl` extracts usage from `type:turn.completed`, mapping `cached_input_tokens` → `cached_in`
- [ ] Existing flat-format fallback (`role:assistant`) still works
- [ ] New unit test with real Codex JSONL format passes
- [ ] All existing unit tests still pass
